{
  "$comment": "EXP-1507 (eMCP local hub, epic EXP-1503, 2026-10-31): ONE LOOPBACK ENDPOINT OVER SEVERAL MCP SERVERS, the device-side twin of `/api/mcp/apps`. A hub MOUNTS servers under a name (`serverNamePattern`: lowercase letters, digits and `-`, starting with a letter or digit, at most `serverNameMax`; never `__`, the separator), each an upstream MCP server (Streamable HTTP, the run's headers resolved) or an in-process tool provider; mounting a name twice replaces it. NAMING: the hub lists a mounted tool as exposes.json's qualified name with the SERVER NAME in place of the app slug (`qualifiedToolName(server, tool)`, `<server>__<tool>`, cut + hashed past 64) and resolves a call with `splitToolName` against the run's own list, so a tool whose own name holds `__` is never listed; servers are listed sorted by name and a qualified name an earlier server holds is dropped (`listToolNames`; within a server its own order). GRANTS (`listCases`): the hub admits a RUN with its own bearer token (an earlier token of the run dies; a revoke kills it) and a GRANT: `servers` = server name -> level (`read` | `write`; a server not named = `none`), plus the `teamId` and `userId` the run acts for (null on a device with no team). A tool's access is exposes.json's `upstreamAccess(annotations)` (read iff `readOnlyHint: true`, else write: destructive tools need write like every other); a tool is LISTED and CALLABLE iff access.json's `toolVisible(level, access)`. A CALL (`callCases`) to a name not on the run's list answers MCP's unknown-tool error (JSON-RPC -32602), never a hint that it exists, and is audited `denied` with error `unknownTool`; a listed call reaches its server once, as `tool` with the arguments as received. AUDIT: EVERY tools/call, denied ones included, writes ONE `mcp_calls` row (audit.json's columns, handed to the host's sink after the call, never blocking it): `id` a fresh uuid, `team_id` / `user_id` = the grant's, `client_id` = the run's session id (on a device the run is the client), `app_id` null, `tool` = the name as called, `status` = audit.json's `callStatus` of the outcome, `error` = `errors[outcome]` (null for `ok` and `isError`), `latency_ms` = the hub's wall time rounded down, `args_hash` = audit.json's `argsHash` of the arguments as received, `created_at` = ISO-8601 UTC with milliseconds. Outcomes (`outcomes`): `ok` = a result; `isError` = a result with `isError: true` -> failed; `invalidParams` = the server answered JSON-RPC -32602 -> invalid; `rpcError` = any other JSON-RPC error, `unreachable` = no connection or an HTTP error, `timeout` = no answer in time -> upstream; `unknown` = not listed for the run -> denied. Retention is the host's (audit.json `retentionDays`).",
  "serverNamePattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$",
  "serverNameMax": 32,
  "outcomes": {
    "ok": "ok",
    "isError": "failed",
    "invalidParams": "invalid",
    "rpcError": "upstream",
    "unreachable": "upstream",
    "timeout": "upstream",
    "unknown": "denied"
  },
  "errors": {
    "ok": null,
    "isError": null,
    "invalidParams": "invalidArguments",
    "rpcError": "upstreamFailed",
    "unreachable": "upstreamFailed",
    "timeout": "upstreamTimeout",
    "unknown": "unknownTool"
  },
  "unknownToolCode": -32602,
